<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Taizu of Liao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">872–926</span> · Also known as Yelü Abaoji, Abaoji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yelü Abaoji, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Taizu</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, was the Khitan leader who founded the Liao dynasty. Chosen as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> around 907, he broke with the custom of rotating leadership, proclaimed himself emperor in 916 and built a state combining steppe and Chinese institutions, including a Khitan script. He conquered the kingdom of Balhae in 926 and died on the way home.</p></div>
